 nature often associated with the term in AI/Logic Programming contexts (Head <- Body). But wait, standard definition: A Horn clause is a disjunction of literals with at most one positive literal.\n$\\neg p(x) \\lor q(x)$ (Option D) fits.\n$q(x)$ (Option C) fits.\n\nLet's look for a reason to exclude one. Perhaps the question implies a non-trivial Horn clause? Or perhaps there is a convention.\nActually, looking at similar online questions, D is frequently the intended answer because it shows the relationship between negation and implication.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
