      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumTime(s: str) -> str:\n    # Convert to list for mutability\n    chars = list(s)\n    \n    # Handle hours tens digit (index 0)\n    if chars[0] == '?':\n        # If units digit is '?' or <= '1', then tens can be '1'\n        # If units digit is > '1', then tens must be '0' because max hour is 11\n        if chars[1] == '?' or chars[1] <= '1':\n            chars[0] = '1'\n        else:\n            chars[0] = '0'\n    \n    # Handle hours units digit (index 1)\n    if chars[1] == '?':\n        # If tens digit is '1', units can be at most '1' (so max is 11)\n        # If tens digit is '0', units can be up to '9' (so max is 09)\n        if chars[0] == '1':\n            chars[1] = '1'\n        else:\n            chars[1] = '9'\n    \n    # Handle minutes tens digit (index 3)\n    if chars[3] == '?':\n        # Minutes tens digit can be at most '5'\n        chars[3] = '5'\n    \n    # Handle minutes units digit (index 4)\n    if chars[4] == '?':\n        # Minutes units digit can be at most '9'\n        chars[4] = '9'\n    \n    return \"\".join(chars)\n```",
