#       Why the difference?\n        #       Because if odd_count == 0, we can't pick a d with odd freq. We must pick a d with even freq.\n        #       Then max_sum = n - 1.\n        #       If odd_count > 0, we can pick d with odd freq.\n        #       Then max_sum = n - odd_count + 1.\n        \n        #   So:\n        #   if m % 2 == 0:\n        #     return YES if k >= odd_count else NO\n        #   else:\n        #     if odd_count > 0:\n        #       return YES if k >= odd_count - 1 else NO\n        #     else:\n        #       return YES if k >= 1 else NO\n        \n        # Let's verify with samples.\n        # Sample 1: n=1, k=0, s=\"a\". odd_count=1. m=1 (odd). odd_count>0. k >= 0? 0 >= 0. YES. Correct.\n        # Sample 2: n=2, k=0, s=\"ab\". odd_count=2. m=2 (even). k >= 2? 0 >= 2. NO. Correct.\n        # Sample 3: n=2, k=1, s=\"ba\". odd_count=2. m=1 (odd). odd_count>0. k >= 1? 1 >= 1. YES. Correct.\n        # Sample 4: n=3, k=1, s=\"abb\". freq: a:1, b:2. odd_count=1. m=2 (even). k >= 1? 1 >= 1. YES. Correct.\n        # Sample 5: n=3, k=2, s=\"abc\". freq: a:1, b:1, c:1. odd_count=3. m=1 (odd). odd_count>0. k >= 2? 2 >= 2. YES. Correct.\n        # Sample 6: n=6, k=2, s=\"bacacd\". freq: a:2, b:1, c:2, d:1. odd_count=2 (b,d). m=4 (even). k >= 2? 2 >= 2. YES. Correct.\n        # Sample 7: n=6, k=2, s=\"fagbza\". freq: a:2, b:1, f:1, g:1, z:1. odd_count=4. m=4 (even). k >= 4? 2 >= 4. NO. Correct.\n        # Sample 8: n=6, k=2, s=\"zwaafa\". freq: a:3, f:1, w:1, z:1. odd_count=4. m=4 (even). k >= 4? 2 >= 4. NO. Correct.\n        # Sample 9: n=7, k=2, s=\"taagaak\". freq: a:3, g:1, k:1, t:1. odd_count=4. m=5 (odd). odd_count>0. k >= 3? 2 >= 3. NO.\n        # Wait, sample output says YES for 9th test case.\n        # Let's re-check sample 9.\n        # s=\"taagaak\", n=7, k=2. m=5.\n        # freq: t:1, a:3, g:1, k:1. odd_count=4.\n        # My logic: m is odd, odd_count>0, check k >= odd_count - 1 = 3.\n        # k=2, so 2 >= 3 is False. Output NO.\