      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef doesValidArrayExist(derived: list[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determine whether there exists a valid binary array 'original' that could have formed 'derived'.\n    \n    The derived array is formed by:\n    derived[i] = original[i] XOR original[(i+1) % n]\n    \n    Key Insight:\n    XORing all elements of the derived array:\n    derived[0] ^ derived[1] ^ ... ^ derived[n-1]\n    = (original[0]^original[1]) ^ (original[1]^original[2]) ^ ... ^ (original[n-1]^original[0])\n    \n    Each element of original appears exactly twice in this expansion.\n    Since x ^ x = 0 for any bit x, the total XOR sum must be 0.\n    \n    Therefore, a valid original array exists if and only if the XOR sum of all elements in derived is 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    xor_sum = 0\n    for val in derived:\n        xor_sum ^= val\n    return xor_sum == 0\n```",
