    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef longest_valid_substring(word: str, forbidden: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the length of the longest valid substring of 'word'.\n    A substring is valid if it does not contain any string from 'forbidden' as a substring.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(word)\n    # Convert forbidden list to a set for O(1) lookup\n    forbidden_set = set(forbidden)\n    \n    # We will use a sliding window approach.\n    # left and right define the current window [left, right).\n    # We want to find the maximum (right - left) such that word[left:right] is valid.\n    \n    max_len = 0\n    left = 0\n    \n    # To efficiently check validity, we can iterate right from 0 to n.\n    # For each right, we ensure that the window [left, right] does not contain any forbidden string.\n    # When we add word[right], we need to check if adding this character creates a forbidden substring ending at right.\n    # If it does, we must move left forward until the forbidden substring is no longer in the window.\n    \n    # Optimization: Since forbidden strings have max length 10, we only need to check substrings ending at 'right'\n    # with lengths from 1 to min(10, right - left + 1).\n    \n    for right in range(n):\n        # Check if any forbidden string ends at index 'right' within the current window.\n        # The possible endings are at indices: right, right-1, ..., right-9 (since max forbidden length is 10)\n        # But they must start at or after 'left'.\n        \n        # We check lengths from 1 up to 10 (or until the start of the substring would be before 'left')\n        for length in range(1, 11):\n            if right - length + 1 < left:\n                break\n            \n            substring = word[right - length + 1 : right + 1]\n            if substring in forbidden_set:\n                # This forbidden substring is now in our window [left, right+1).\n                # We need to move left past the start of this forbidden substring.\n                # The forbidden substring starts at right - length + 1.\n                # So the new left should be right - length + 2 (to exclude the first char of the forbidden substring).\n                left = right - length + 2\n                break\n        \n        # Now the window [left, right+1] is valid.\n        current_len = right - left + 1\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            \n    return max_len\n```",
