      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minExtraChar(s: str, dictionary: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the minimum number of extra characters left over if you break up s optimally\n    such that each substring is present in dictionary.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    word_set = set(dictionary)\n    \n    # dp[i] represents the minimum extra characters in the prefix s[0:i]\n    # i ranges from 0 to n\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    \n    # Base case: dp[0] = 0, no extra characters in empty string\n    \n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # Option 1: The character s[i-1] is an extra character\n        dp[i] = dp[i - 1] + 1\n        \n        # Option 2: Try to match a word ending at index i-1\n        for length in range(1, i + 1):\n            start_index = i - length\n            substring = s[start_index:i]\n            if substring in word_set:\n                dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[start_index])\n                \n    return dp[n]\n```",
