      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    H = int(input_data[0])\n    W = int(input_data[1])\n    \n    grid = []\n    for i in range(2, 2 + H):\n        grid.append(list(input_data[i]))\n    \n    # Track which positions are still present\n    # We can use a set of (r, c) for remaining cookies, or a boolean matrix\n    # Since H, W <= 2000, a boolean matrix is efficient enough.\n    \n    remaining = [[True] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    \n    while True:\n        to_remove = set()\n        \n        # Step 1: Check rows\n        for r in range(H):\n            # Count remaining cookies in this row\n            count = 0\n            colors = {}\n            for c in range(W):\n                if remaining[r][c]:\n                    count += 1\n                    ch = grid[r][c]\n                    colors[ch] = colors.get(ch, 0) + 1\n            \n            # If there are two or more cookies remaining AND they all have the same color\n            if count >= 2:\n                # Check if all remaining cookies in this row have the same color\n                # This means only one key in colors dict, and its value == count\n                if len(colors) == 1:\n                    for c in range(W):\n                        if remaining[r][c]:\n                            to_remove.add((r, c))\n        \n        # Step 2: Check columns\n        for c in range(W):\n            count = 0\n            colors = {}\n            for r in range(H):\n                if remaining[r][c]:\n                    count += 1\n                    ch = grid[r][c]\n                    colors[ch] = colors.get(ch, 0) + 1\n            \n            if count >= 2:\n                if len(colors) == 1:\n                    for r in range(H):\n                        if remaining[r][c]:\n                            to_remove.add((r, c))\n        \n        # Step 3: Remove marked cookies\n        if not to_remove:\n            break\n        \n        for (r, c) in to_remove:\n            remaining[r][c] = False\n    \n    # Count remaining cookies\n    ans = 0\n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            if remaining[r][c]:\n                ans += 1\n                \n    print(ans)\n\nsolve()\n```",
