      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    \n    # An Extended ABC string is formed by concatenating:\n    # S_A (all 'A's, possibly empty) + S_B (all 'B's, possibly empty) + S_C (all 'C's, possibly empty)\n    # So the string must look like: A...A B...B C...C\n    # Where each part can be empty.\n    \n    # We can check this by ensuring that once we switch from A to B, we never go back to A.\n    # Once we switch from B to C, we never go back to B or A.\n    # Also, we can't have B before A, or C before B, etc.\n    \n    # More simply: the string should match the regex ^A*B*C*$\n    \n    import re\n    if re.fullmatch(r'A*B*C*', s):\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
