    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_172",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given a string s that consists of lowercase English letters.\nA string is called special if it is made up of only a single character. For example, the string \"abc\" is not special, whereas the strings \"ddd\", \"zz\", and \"f\" are special.\nReturn the length of the longest special substring of s which occurs at least thrice, or -1 if no special substring occurs at least thrice.\nA substring is a contiguous non-empty sequence of characters within a string.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: s = \"aaaa\"\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: The longest special substring which occurs thrice is \"aa\": substrings \"aaaa\", \"aaaa\", and \"aaaa\".\nIt can be shown that the maximum length achievable is 2.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: s = \"abcdef\"\nOutput: -1\nExplanation: There exists no special substring which occurs at least thrice. Hence return -1.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: s = \"abcaba\"\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: The longest special substring which occurs thrice is \"a\": substrings \"abcaba\", \"abcaba\", and \"abcaba\".\nIt can be shown that the maximum length achievable is 1.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n3 <= s.length <= 50\ns consists of only lowercase English letters.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve(s: str) -> int:\n    # We need to find the longest special substring (single char repeated)\n    # that appears at least 3 times in s.\n    \n    # First, let's identify all maximal consecutive segments of identical characters.\n    # For each segment of length L consisting of character c, it contributes\n    # multiple special substrings of character c with lengths 1, 2, ..., L.\n    # Specifically, a segment of length L contains:\n    #   (L - k + 1) substrings of length k (for k from 1 to L).\n    \n    # Instead of iterating all substrings, we can count how many times each\n    # special substring of length k occurs.\n    \n    # Let's use a frequency map: count[(char, length)] = number of occurrences\n    \n    from collections import defaultdict\n    \n    counts = defaultdict(int)\n    \n    n = len(s)\n    i = 0\n    while i < n:\n        j = i\n        while j < n and s[j] == s[i]:\n            j += 1\n        # Segment from i to j-1, length = j - i, character = s[i]\n        length = j - i\n        char = s[i]\n        \n        # This segment of length `length` contributes to special substrings of character `char`\n        # with lengths 1, 2, ..., length.\n        # For a target length k (1 <= k <= length), the number of substrings of length k \n        # in this segment is (length - k + 1).\n        for k in range(1, length + 1):\n            counts[(char, k)] += (length - k + 1)\n        \n        i = j\n    \n    # Now find the maximum k such that there exists some char where counts[(char, k)] >= 3\n    result = -1\n    for char in 'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz':\n        for k in range(1, 51):  # max length is 50\n            if counts[(char, k)] >= 3:\n                result = max(result, k)\n    \n    return result\n```",
