    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef furthestPointFromOrigin(moves: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the furthest distance from the origin that can be reached.\n    \n    Args:\n        moves: A string containing 'L', 'R', and '_' characters representing moves.\n        \n    Returns:\n        The maximum absolute distance from the origin achievable.\n    \"\"\"\n    l_count = moves.count('L')\n    r_count = moves.count('R')\n    underscore_count = moves.count('_')\n    \n    # To maximize distance to the left:\n    # All 'L's go left, all 'R's go right, all '_'s can go left.\n    # Net position = (underscore_count + l_count) - r_count\n    \n    # To maximize distance to the right:\n    # All 'R's go right, all 'L's go left, all '_'s can go right.\n    # Net position = (underscore_count + r_count) - l_count\n    \n    max_left = underscore_count + l_count - r_count\n    max_right = underscore_count + r_count - l_count\n    \n    return max(abs(max_left), abs(max_right))\n```",
