      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findShortestNonSubstring(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the shortest substring of each string in arr that does not occur as a substring\n    in any other string in arr. If multiple such substrings exist, return the lexicographically smallest.\n    If no such substring exists, return an empty string for that position.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    answer = []\n    \n    # Precompute all substrings present in each string\n    # substrings_in[i] will be a set of all substrings of arr[i]\n    substrings_in = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        s = arr[i]\n        subs = set()\n        length = len(s)\n        for start in range(length):\n            for end in range(start + 1, length + 1):\n                subs.add(s[start:end])\n        substrings_in.append(subs)\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        current_s = arr[i]\n        current_subs = substrings_in[i]\n        \n        # Collect all substrings that appear in OTHER strings\n        other_substrings = set()\n        for j in range(n):\n            if i != j:\n                other_substrings.update(substrings_in[j])\n        \n        # Find all substrings of current_s that are NOT in other_substrings\n        candidates = []\n        length = len(current_s)\n        for start in range(length):\n            for end in range(start + 1, length + 1):\n                sub = current_s[start:end]\n                if sub not in other_substrings:\n                    candidates.append(sub)\n        \n        if not candidates:\n            answer.append(\"\")\n        else:\n            # Sort by length first, then lexicographically\n            candidates.sort(key=lambda x: (len(x), x))\n            answer.append(candidates[0])\n    \n    return answer\n```",
