    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n\n    iterator = iter(input_data)\n    \n    try:\n        N = int(next(iterator))\n        M = int(next(iterator))\n    except StopIteration:\n        return\n\n    # Adjacency list: graph[u] contains list of (v, dx, dy)\n    # This means person v is at (dx, dy) relative to person u.\n    # So if pos[u] = (xu, yu), then pos[v] = (xu + dx, yu + dy).\n    graph = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    \n    for _ in range(M):\n        A = int(next(iterator))\n        B = int(next(iterator))\n        X = int(next(iterator))\n        Y = int(next(iterator))\n        \n        # From A's perspective, B is at (X, Y).\n        # So pos[B] = pos[A] + (X, Y)\n        # Edge A -> B with weight (X, Y)\n        graph[A].append((B, X, Y))\n        \n        # Also add reverse edge for traversal if needed, though we just need connected components.\n        # From B's perspective, A is at (-X, -Y).\n        graph[B].append((A, -X, -Y))\n\n    # Person 1 is at the origin (0, 0).\n    # We will determine coordinates for each connected component containing Person 1.\n    # For other components, coordinates are undecidable because we have no absolute reference.\n    \n    # Initialize coordinates array with None\n    coords = [None] * (N + 1)\n    coords[1] = (0, 0)\n    \n    # BFS/DFS starting from Node 1 to resolve coordinates within its component\n    stack = [1]\n    visited_in_component = {1}\n    \n    while stack:\n        u = stack.pop()\n        xu, yu = coords[u]\n        \n        for v, dx, dy in graph[u]:\n            if v not in visited_in_component:\n                # Determine coordinate of v\n                xv = xu + dx\n                yv = yu + dy\n                coords[v] = (xv, yv)\n                visited_in_component.add(v)\n                stack.append(v)\n            else:\n                # Consistency check (though problem states input is consistent)\n                pass\n                \n    # Check which nodes are decidable.\n    # A node is decidable if it is in the same connected component as Node 1.\n    # Since we started BFS from 1, any node whose coord is not None is decidable.\n    # Nodes not reachable from 1 will have coords[i] == None.\n    \n    output_lines = []\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        if coords[i] is not None:\n            sx, sy = coords[i]\n            output_lines.append(f\"{sx} {sy}\")\n        else:\n            output_lines.append(\"undecidable\")\n            \n    print('\\n'.join(output_lines))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    solve()\n```",
