      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    s = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    t = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    \n    # Method 1: Take a subsequence of length 3 from S, convert to uppercase, check if equals T\n    # We need to find if there exist indices i < j < k such that \n    # s[i].upper() == T[0], s[j].upper() == T[1], s[k].upper() == T[2]\n    \n    def find_subsequence_3(s, t):\n        # Find first character of T in S\n        idx1 = -1\n        for i in range(len(s)):\n            if s[i].upper() == t[0]:\n                idx1 = i\n                break\n        \n        if idx1 == -1:\n            return False\n        \n        # Find second character of T in S after idx1\n        idx2 = -1\n        for i in range(idx1 + 1, len(s)):\n            if s[i].upper() == t[1]:\n                idx2 = i\n                break\n        \n        if idx2 == -1:\n            return False\n        \n        # Find third character of T in S after idx2\n        idx3 = -1\n        for i in range(idx2 + 1, len(s)):\n            if s[i].upper() == t[2]:\n                idx3 = i\n                break\n        \n        return idx3 != -1\n    \n    # Method 2: Take a subsequence of length 2 from S, convert to uppercase, append 'X' to form T\n    # So T must end with 'X', and the first two characters of T must be found as a subsequence in S\n    def find_subsequence_2_with_x(s, t):\n        # Check if T ends with 'X'\n        if t[2] != 'X':\n            return False\n        \n        # Find first character of T[0] in S\n        idx1 = -1\n        for i in range(len(s)):\n            if s[i].upper() == t[0]:\n                idx1 = i\n                break\n        \n        if idx1 == -1:\n            return False\n        \n        # Find second character of T[1] in S after idx1\n        idx2 = -1\n        for i in range(idx1 + 1, len(s)):\n            if s[i].upper() == t[1]:\n                idx2 = i\n                break\n        \n        return idx2 != -1\n    \n    if find_subsequence_3(s, t) or find_subsequence_2_with_x(s, t):\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
