      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumHappinessSum(happiness: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the maximum sum of happiness values of selected children.\n    \n    Args:\n        happiness: List of integers representing happiness values of children.\n        k: Number of children to select.\n        \n    Returns:\n        Maximum sum of happiness values of the selected children.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Sort the happiness values in descending order to prioritize higher values\n    happiness.sort(reverse=True)\n    \n    total_happiness = 0\n    \n    # Select the top k children\n    for i in range(k):\n        # Each time we pick a child, all previously unselected children's happiness decreases by 1\n        # So the i-th child picked (0-indexed) will have their original happiness reduced by i\n        current_happiness = max(0, happiness[i] - i)\n        total_happiness += current_happiness\n        \n    return total_happiness\n```",
