    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nThere is an infinitely long piano keyboard.\nIs there a continuous segment within this keyboard that consists of W white keys and B black keys?\n\nLet S be the string formed by infinitely repeating the string wbwbwwbwbwbw.\nIs there a substring of S that consists of W occurrences of w and B occurrences of b?\n\nWhat is a substring of S?\nA substring of S is a string that can be formed by concatenating the l-th, (l+1)-th, \\dots, r-th characters of S in this order for some two positive integers l and r (l\\leq r).\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nW B\n\nOutput\n\nIf there is a substring of S that consists of W occurrences of w and B occurrences of b, print Yes; otherwise, print No.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- W and B are integers.\n- 0\\leq W,B \\leq 100\n- W+B \\geq 1\n\nSample Input 1\n\n3 2\n\nSample Output 1\n\nYes\n\nThe first 15 characters of S are wbwbwwbwbwbwwbw. You can take the 11-th through 15-th characters to form the string bwwbw, which is a substring consisting of three occurrences of w and two occurrences of b.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n3 0\n\nSample Output 2\n\nNo\n\nThe only string consisting of three occurrences of w and zero occurrences of b is www, which is not a substring of S.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n92 66\n\nSample Output 3\n\nYes",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    W = int(input_data[0])\n    B = int(input_data[1])\n    \n    # The pattern repeats every 12 characters: \"wbwbwwbwbwbw\"\n    pattern = \"wbwbwwbwbwbw\"\n    \n    # Since the keyboard is infinitely long and S is periodic,\n    # we need to check if there exists a substring of S with W 'w's and B 'b's.\n    # Because it's periodic, we can just check substrings of S formed by\n    # concatenating enough periods to cover the maximum possible length needed.\n    # Max W+B is 200. The period length is 12. So checking a few periods is enough.\n    # Let's create a large enough string to be safe.\n    # We need to find if there's a contiguous segment with exactly W w's and B b's.\n    \n    # Generate a sufficiently long string from the pattern\n    # The max total characters is 200. One period has 12 chars.\n    # 200 / 12 = ~16.67. So let's generate 20 periods to be very safe.\n    S_large = pattern * 20\n    \n    n = len(S_large)\n    \n    # We want to find if there exists a substring with count_w = W and count_b = B.\n    # Since W, B <= 100, the substring length L = W + B <= 200.\n    # We can iterate over all possible substring lengths L from 1 to W+B.\n    # For each length L, we check if there's a window of size L with W w's and B b's.\n    # But actually, we just need to check windows of size W+B specifically?\n    # No, the problem asks for a substring with EXACTLY W w's and EXACTLY B b's.\n    # So the length must be W+B.\n    \n    target_len = W + B\n    \n    if target_len == 0:\n        # Constraints say W+B >= 1, so this won't happen.\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n        \n    # Check all substrings of length target_len in S_large\n    # Since S_large is long enough, if such a substring exists in the infinite S,\n    # it will appear in S_large.\n    \n    found = False\n    \n    # Precompute counts for sliding window\n    # Count w's and b's in the first window of size target_len\n    if target_len > n:\n        # This shouldn't happen given our S_large size and constraints\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n        \n    current_w = 0\n    current_b = 0\n    for i in range(target_len):\n        if S_large[i] == 'w':\n            current_w += 1\n        else:\n            current_b += 1\n            \n    if current_w == W and current_b == B:\n        found = True\n    else:\n        for i in range(1, n - target_len + 1):\n            # Remove character at i-1\n            out_char = S_large[i-1]\n            if out_char == 'w':\n                current_w -= 1\n            else:\n                current_b -= 1\n                \n            # Add character at i+target_len-1\n            in_char = S_large[i+target_len-1]\n            if in_char == 'w':\n                current_w += 1\n            else:\n                current_b += 1\n                \n            if current_w == W and current_b == B:\n                found = True\n                break\n                \n    if found:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
