      "generated_answer": "```python\nclass Solution:\n    def maxSum(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> int:\n        MOD = 10**9 + 7\n        \n        # Count the number of set bits at each position across all numbers\n        bit_count = [0] * 30\n        \n        for num in nums:\n            for i in range(30):\n                if (num >> i) & 1:\n                    bit_count[i] += 1\n        \n        # Construct the k largest possible numbers based on bit counts\n        # We want to maximize the sum of squares, so we should greedily form the largest numbers\n        # For each of the k positions, construct a number by setting bit i if bit_count[i] > 0\n        # Then decrement bit_count[i]\n        \n        result_nums = []\n        for _ in range(k):\n            val = 0\n            for i in range(30):\n                if bit_count[i] > 0:\n                    val |= (1 << i)\n                    bit_count[i] -= 1\n            result_nums.append(val)\n        \n        # Calculate sum of squares modulo MOD\n        total = 0\n        for num in result_nums:\n            total = (total + (num * num) % MOD) % MOD\n            \n        return total\n```",
