      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    \n    if not input_data:\n        return\n\n    iterator = iter(input_data)\n    \n    try:\n        H = int(next(iterator))\n        W = int(next(iterator))\n        T = int(next(iterator))\n    except StopIteration:\n        return\n\n    grid = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        grid.append(next(iterator))\n\n    # Find Start, Goal, and Candies\n    start_pos = None\n    goal_pos = None\n    candies = []\n    \n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            char = grid[r][c]\n            if char == 'S':\n                start_pos = (r, c)\n            elif char == 'G':\n                goal_pos = (r, c)\n            elif char == 'o':\n                candies.append((r, c))\n    \n    n_candies = len(candies)\n    \n    # Map points to indices: Start=0, Goal=n_candies+1, Candies=1..n_candies\n    # We need distances between Start, all Candies, and Goal.\n    # Total points of interest: Start + Candies + Goal\n    \n    points_of_interest = [start_pos] + candies + [goal_pos]\n    num_points = len(points_of_interest)\n    \n    # Precompute distances using BFS from each point of interest\n    # dists[i][j] will store the shortest distance between point i and point j\n    # If unreachable, infinity\n    \n    INF = float('inf')\n    dists = [[INF] * num_points for _ in range(num_points)]\n    \n    # Directions for movement\n    dirs = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n    \n    def bfs(start_node_idx):\n        r0, c0 = points_of_interest[start_node_idx]\n        d = [[INF] * W for _ in range(H)]\n        d[r0][c0] = 0\n        queue = deque([(r0, c0)])\n        \n        while queue:\n            r, c = queue.popleft()\n            \n            for dr, dc in dirs:\n                nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n                if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W:\n                    if grid[nr][nc] != '#' and d[nr][nc] == INF:\n                        d[nr][nc] = d[r][c] + 1\n                        queue.append((nr, nc))\n        \n        # Fill the row in dists for this start_node_idx\n        for j in range(num_points):\n            rj, cj = points_of_interest[j]\n            dists[start_node_idx][j] = d[rj][cj]\n\n    for i in range(num_points):\n        bfs(i)\n        \n    # Check if Start can reach Goal directly within T moves?\n    # Actually, we need to visit some subset of candies.\n    # This is a variation of TSP / Traveling Salesman Problem with constraints.\n    # Since n_candies <= 18, we can use bitmask DP.\n    \n    # State: dp[mask][last_visited_idx]\n    # mask: bitmask representing the set of candies visited.\n    # last_visited_idx: index in points_of_interest of the last visited point.\n    # Note: Points 1 to n_candies are candies. Point 0 is Start. Point n_candies+1 is Goal.\n    \n    # Let's redefine indices for clarity in DP:\n    # 0: Start\n    # 1..n_candies: Candies\n    # n_candies+1: Goal\n    \n    # We want to find max bits set in mask such that there exists a path:\n    # Start -> ... -> Candy (subset defined by mask) -> ... -> Goal\n    # with total length <= T.\n    \n    # However, the order matters.\n    # dp[mask][u] = minimum distance to reach state where candies in 'mask' have been visited,\n    # and the current location is 'u', where u is an index into points_of_interest corresponding to a candy or start.\n    # Specifically, u ranges from 0 to n_candies.\n    # We don't include Goal in the 'last visited' state for the DP transitions because once we go to Goal, we stop.\n    # But wait, the problem says \"visit candy squares on the way to the goal\".\n    # So the path is Start -> [sequence of candies] -> Goal.\n    \n    # Let dp[mask][u] be the min distance starting from Start, visiting exactly the set of candies in 'mask',\n    # and ending at candy/point u. Here u is the index of the last candy visited (1..n_candies).\n    # mask includes u.\n    \n    # Initialize:\n    # For each candy i (1..n_candies):\n    #   if dists[0][i] <= T:\n    #       dp[1<<(i-1)][i] = dists[0][i]\n    #   else:\n    #       dp[1<<(i-1)][i] = INF\n    \n    # If no candies, check if dists[0][Goal] <= T.\n    \n    # Transitions:\n    # Iterate through masks from 1 to 2^n - 1.\n    # For each mask, for each u in mask:\n    #   if dp[mask][u] is INF, continue.\n    #   Try to go to next candy v not in mask:\n    #       new_dist = dp[mask][u] + dists[u][v]\n    #       if new_dist <= T:\n    #           new_mask = mask | (1<<(v-1))\n    #           dp[new_mask][v] = min(dp[new_mask][v], new_dist)\n    \n    # After filling DP, iterate all masks and all u.\n    # Check if we can go from u to Goal:\n    #   total_dist = dp[mask][u] + dists[u][Goal]\n    #   if total_dist <= T:\n    #       update max_candies = max(max_candies, popcount(mask))\n    \n    # Also consider the case where no candies are visited.\n    # If dists[0][Goal] <= T, max_candies = max(max_candies, 0)\n    \n    if n_candies == 0:\n        if dists[0][num_points-1] <= T:\n            print(0)\n        else:\n            print(-1)\n        return\n\n    # DP table\n    # dp[mask][u] where mask is 0..2^n-1, u is 0..n-1 (index in candies list)\n    # To map easier: let's use 0-based indexing for candies in DP array.\n    # Candies are points 1 to n_candies in points_of_interest.\n    # Let candy_index j (0..n-1) correspond to point_of_interest index j+1.\n    \n    num_states = 1 << n_candies\n    # dp[mask][candy_idx]\n    dp = [[INF] * n_candies for _ in range(num_states)]\n    \n    # Base cases: Start -> Candy i\n    start_point_idx = 0\n    goal_point_idx = num_points - 1\n    \n    for i in range(n_candies):\n        p_idx = i + 1\n        d = dists[start_point_idx][p_idx]\n        if d <= T:\n            dp[1 << i][i] = d\n            \n    ans = -1\n    \n    # Check if direct path to goal is possible with 0 candies\n    if dists[start_point_idx][goal_point_idx] <= T:\n        ans = 0\n        \n    # Iterate masks\n    for mask in range(1, num_states):\n        for u in range(n_candies):\n            # If u is not in mask, skip\n            if not (mask & (1 << u)):\n                continue\n            \n            current_dist = dp[mask][u]\n            if current_dist == INF:\n                continue\n            \n            # Try to go to Goal from here\n            # The current last visited candy is u, which corresponds to point_of_interest index u+1\n            p_u = u + 1\n            dist_to_goal = dists[p_u][goal_point_idx]\n            if dist_to_goal != INF and current_dist + dist_to_goal <= T:\n                # Count bits in mask\n                cnt = bin(mask).count('1')\n                if cnt > ans:\n                    ans = cnt\n            \n            # Try to extend to next candy v\n            for v in range(n_candies):\n                if mask & (1 << v):\n                    continue\n                \n                p_v = v + 1\n                dist_uv = dists[p_u][p_v]\n                \n                if dist_uv != INF:\n                    new_dist = current_dist + dist_uv\n                    if new_dist <= T:\n                        new_mask = mask | (1 << v)\n                        if new_dist < dp[new_mask][v]:\n                            dp[new_mask][v] = new_dist\n\n    print(ans)\n\nsolve()\n```",
