      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to determine if two numbers on a 3×3 grid are horizontally adjacent.\n\n**Grid layout:**\n```\n1 2 3\n4 5 6\n7 8 9\n```\n\n**Horizontal adjacency pairs:** (1,2), (2,3), (4,5), (5,6), (7,8), (8,9)\n\nThese are exactly the pairs where `B - A == 1` and both numbers are in the same row (i.e., they don't straddle a multiple of 3 boundary). The condition `A % 3 != 0` ensures A is not the rightmost cell of its row (3 or 6), and `B - A == 1` ensures they are consecutive.\n\n**Examples verification:**\n- 7 8: 7%3=1≠0, 8-7=1 → Yes ✓\n- 1 9: |1-9|=8≠1 → No ✓\n- 3 4: 3%3=0, fails first check → No ✓\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    A, B = map(int, input().split())\n    if abs(A - B) == 1 and A % 3 != 0:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```\n\nThe solution:\n1. Reads A and B from input\n2. Checks if they are consecutive (`abs(A - B) == 1`)\n3. Checks if A is not in the rightmost column (`A % 3 != 0`) — this prevents pairs like (3,4) which are vertically adjacent, not horizontally\n4. Prints \"Yes\" if both conditions hold, \"No\" otherwise",
