    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef semiOrderedPermutation(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    n = len(nums)\n    pos_1 = nums.index(1)\n    pos_n = nums.index(n)\n    \n    # Number of swaps to move 1 to index 0 is pos_1\n    # Number of swaps to move n to index n-1 is (n - 1 - pos_n)\n    \n    # However, if 1 is originally to the right of n, moving 1 to the left will shift n's position by 1.\n    # Specifically, if pos_1 > pos_n, then when we swap 1 past n, n moves one index to the left.\n    # So we save one swap for n.\n    \n    ops = pos_1 + (n - 1 - pos_n)\n    \n    if pos_1 > pos_n:\n        ops -= 1\n        \n    return ops\n```",
