    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. The function should take stdin as input and print the output. Simply call the function after the definition. Question:\nThere are N cities in a certain country.\nYou will travel from your office in city 1 to a destination in city N, via zero or more cities.\nTwo types of transportation are available: company car and train. The time required to travel from city i to city j is as follows:\n\n- D_{{i,j}} \\times A minutes by company car, and\n- D_{{i,j}} \\times B + C minutes by train.\n\nYou can switch from company car to train, but not vice versa.\nYou can do so without spending time, but only in a city.\nWhat is the minimum time in minutes to travel from city 1 to city N?\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN A B C\nD_{{1,1}} D_{{1,2}} \\ldots D_{{1,N}}\nD_{{2,1}} D_{{2,2}} \\ldots D_{{2,N}}\n\\vdots\nD_{{N,1}} D_{{N,2}} \\ldots D_{{N,N}}\n\nOutput\n\nPrint the answer as an integer.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 2 \\leq N \\leq 1000\n- 1 \\leq A, B, C \\leq 10^6 \n- D_{{i,j}} \\leq 10^6\n- D_{{i,i}} = 0\n- D_{{i,j}} = D_{{j,i}} > 0 (i \\neq j)\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n4 8 5 13\n0 6 2 15\n6 0 3 5\n2 3 0 13\n15 5 13 0\n\nSample Output 1\n\n78\n\nYou can travel from city 1 to city 4 in a total of 78 minutes by moving as follows.\n\n- Travel by company car from city 1 to city 3. This takes 2 \\times 8 = 16 minutes.\n- Travel by company car from city 3 to city 2. This takes 3 \\times 8 = 24 minutes.\n- Travel by train from city 2 to city 4. This takes 5 \\times 5 + 13 = 38 minutes.\n\nIt is impossible to travel from city 1 to city 4 in less than 78 minutes.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n3 1 1000000 1000000\n0 10 1\n10 0 10\n1 10 0\n\nSample Output 2\n\n1\n\nSample Input 3\n\n5 954257 954213 814214\n0 84251 214529 10017 373342\n84251 0 91926 32336 164457\n214529 91926 0 108914 57762\n10017 32336 108914 0 234705\n373342 164457 57762 234705 0\n\nSample Output 3\n\n168604826785",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nimport heapq\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n\n    iterator = iter(input_data)\n    \n    try:\n        N = int(next(iterator))\n        A = int(next(iterator))\n        B = int(next(iterator))\n        C = int(next(iterator))\n        \n        D = []\n        for i in range(N):\n            row = []\n            for j in range(N):\n                row.append(int(next(iterator)))\n            D.append(row)\n    except StopIteration:\n        return\n\n    # We need to find the shortest path from city 1 (index 0) to city N (index N-1).\n    # State can be represented as (city_index, mode).\n    # Mode 0: Using company car.\n    # Mode 1: Using train.\n    # Transition:\n    # - From (u, 0) to (v, 0): cost D[u][v] * A\n    # - From (u, 1) to (v, 1): cost D[u][v] * B + C\n    # - From (u, 0) to (u, 1): cost 0 (switch at city u)\n    # - Cannot switch from train to car.\n\n    # Dijkstra's algorithm\n    # dist[city][mode] stores the minimum time to reach city with given mode\n    INF = float('inf')\n    dist = [[INF, INF] for _ in range(N)]\n    \n    # Start at city 0 (city 1), mode 0 (car) with time 0.\n    # Note: We start with the car. Can we start with train? \n    # \"You can switch from company car to train... only in a city.\"\n    # This implies you start with the company car at city 1.\n    # However, technically you could switch immediately at city 1 to train mode before leaving.\n    # So initial state is city 0, mode 0, time 0.\n    \n    heap = [(0, 0, 0)] # (time, city_idx, mode)\n    dist[0][0] = 0\n    \n    while heap:\n        d, u, mode = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        \n        if d > dist[u][mode]:\n            continue\n            \n        # If we reached destination city N-1, we can consider updating answer, \n        # but we continue to ensure optimality for all paths.\n        \n        # Option 1: Switch from car to train at current city u\n        if mode == 0:\n            new_time = d\n            if new_time < dist[u][1]:\n                dist[u][1] = new_time\n                heapq.heappush(heap, (new_time, u, 1))\n        \n        # Option 2: Travel to neighbor v\n        for v in range(N):\n            if u == v:\n                continue\n            weight = D[u][v]\n            \n            if mode == 0: # Currently in car\n                new_time = d + weight * A\n                if new_time < dist[v][0]:\n                    dist[v][0] = new_time\n                    heapq.heappush(heap, (new_time, v, 0))\n            elif mode == 1: # Currently in train\n                new_time = d + weight * B + C\n                if new_time < dist[v][1]:\n                    dist[v][1] = new_time\n                    heapq.heappush(heap, (new_time, v, 1))\n\n    # The answer is the minimum time to reach city N-1 (index N-1) in either mode\n    ans = min(dist[N-1][0], dist[N-1][1])\n    print(ans)\n\nsolve()\n```",
