      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    H = int(input_data[0])\n    W = int(input_data[1])\n    \n    S = []\n    for i in range(2, 2 + H):\n        S.append(input_data[i])\n        \n    # Directions for step: (dr, dc)\n    # Must be contiguous (sharing side or corner), so dr in [-1, 0, 1], dc in [-1, 0, 1]\n    # But not both 0.\n    # Also, the centers must be on a common line at regular intervals.\n    # This implies that the vector from A_i to A_{i+1} is constant for all i=1..4.\n    # Let the step be (dr, dc). Then:\n    # A_2 = A_1 + (dr, dc)\n    # A_3 = A_1 + 2*(dr, dc)\n    # A_4 = A_1 + 3*(dr, dc)\n    # A_5 = A_1 + 4*(dr, dc)\n    \n    target = ['s', 'n', 'u', 'k', 'e']\n    \n    # Possible steps (dr, dc)\n    steps = []\n    for dr in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for dc in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            if dr == 0 and dc == 0:\n                continue\n            steps.append((dr, dc))\n            \n    found = False\n    result = []\n    \n    for r1 in range(H):\n        for c1 in range(W):\n            if S[r1][c1] != 's':\n                continue\n                \n            for dr, dc in steps:\n                # Check if all 5 positions are within bounds and match target letters\n                positions = []\n                valid = True\n                for i in range(5):\n                    r = r1 + i * dr\n                    c = c1 + i * dc\n                    \n                    if not (0 <= r < H and 0 <= c < W):\n                        valid = False\n                        break\n                        \n                    if S[r][c] != target[i]:\n                        valid = False\n                        break\n                        \n                    positions.append((r + 1, c + 1)) # 1-indexed\n                \n                if valid:\n                    result = positions\n                    found = True\n                    break\n            if found:\n                break\n        if found:\n            break\n            \n    for pos in result:\n        print(f\"{pos[0]} {pos[1]}\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
