    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef distinctDifferenceArray(nums: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    n = len(nums)\n    diff = []\n    \n    # Precompute suffix distinct counts\n    # suffix_distinct[i] will store the number of distinct elements in nums[i+1:]\n    suffix_distinct = [0] * n\n    seen_suffix = set()\n    \n    # Build suffix distinct counts from right to left\n    # For index i, the suffix is nums[i+1...n-1]\n    # We can compute this by iterating backwards.\n    # suffix_distinct[i] depends on nums[i+1:].\n    \n    # Let's compute a helper array where right_distinct[i] = distinct count in nums[i:]\n    right_distinct = [0] * (n + 1)  # right_distinct[n] = 0 (empty suffix)\n    seen = set()\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        seen.add(nums[i])\n        right_distinct[i] = len(seen)\n    \n    # Now, for each index i:\n    # prefix distinct count: distinct elements in nums[0...i]\n    # suffix distinct count: distinct elements in nums[i+1...n-1] = right_distinct[i+1]\n    \n    seen_prefix = set()\n    result = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        seen_prefix.add(nums[i])\n        prefix_count = len(seen_prefix)\n        suffix_count = right_distinct[i + 1]\n        result.append(prefix_count - suffix_count)\n        \n    return result\n```",
