 time are 2001 points for player 1, 1502 points for player 2, and 1703 points for player 3.\nPlayer 1 is already ahead of all other players' total scores without solving any more problems.\nPlayer 2 can, for example, solve problem 4 to have a total score of 3502 points, which would exceed all other players' total scores.\nPlayer 3 can also, for example, solve problem 4 to have a total score of 3703 points, which would exceed all other players' total scores.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n5 5\n1000 1500 2000 2000 2500\nxxxxx\noxxxx\nxxxxx\noxxxx\noxxxx\n\nSample Output 2\n\n1\n1\n1\n1\n0\n\nSample Input 3\n\n7 8\n500 500 500 500 500 500 500 500\nxxxxxxxx\noxxxxxxx\nooxxxxxx\noooxxxxx\nooooxxxx\noooooxxx\nooooooxx\n\nSample Output 3\n\n7\n6\n5\n4\n3\n2\n0",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    iterator = iter(input_data)\n    \n    N = int(next(iterator))\n    M = int(next(iterator))\n    \n    A = []\n    for _ in range(M):\n        A.append(int(next(iterator)))\n        \n    S = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        S.append(next(iterator))\n        \n    # Calculate current total scores for all players\n    # Score for player i (1-indexed in problem description, but 0-indexed in list)\n    # Total score = sum of solved problems' scores + (i+1) points bonus\n    \n    current_scores = []\n    for i in range(N):\n        score = 0\n        for j in range(M):\n            if S[i][j] == 'o':\n                score += A[j]\n        # Bonus is i+1 because player indices are 1..N\n        score += (i + 1)\n        current_scores.append(score)\n        \n    results = []\n    \n    for i in range(N):\n        my_score = current_scores[i]\n        max_other_score = -1\n        \n        # Find the maximum score among all OTHER players\n        for j in range(N):\n            if i != j:\n                if current_scores[j] > max_other_score:\n                    max_other_score = current_scores[j]\n        \n        # Player i needs to solve some unsolved problems to exceed max_other_score\n        # Unsolved problems for player i\n        unsolved_indices = []\n        for j in range(M):\n            if S[i][j] == 'x':\n                unsolved_indices.append(j)\n        \n        # Sort unsolved problems by score descending to minimize count\n        # We want to pick the highest scoring problems first\n        unsolved_scores = [A[j] for j in unsolved_indices]\n        combined = list(zip(unsolved_scores, unsolved_indices))\n        combined.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n        \n        needed_count = 0\n        current_total = my_score\n        target = max_other_score + 1 # Must strictly exceed\n        \n        for score_val, idx in combined:\n            if current_total >= target:\n                break\n            current_total += score_val\n            needed_count += 1\n            \n        results.append(needed_count)\n        \n    for res in results:\n        print(res)\n\nsolve()\n```",
