      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    n = int(sys.stdin.read().strip())\n    \n    # Water stations are at 0, 5, 10, ..., 100\n    # We need to find the multiple of 5 closest to n\n    \n    # Calculate the two candidates: floor(n/5)*5 and ceil(n/5)*5\n    lower = (n // 5) * 5\n    upper = lower + 5\n    \n    # Determine which is closer\n    dist_lower = abs(n - lower)\n    dist_upper = abs(n - upper)\n    \n    if dist_lower <= dist_upper:\n        print(lower)\n    else:\n        print(upper)\n\nsolve()\n```",
