      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n\n    H = int(input_data[0])\n    W = int(input_data[1])\n    K = int(input_data[2])\n    \n    S = input_data[3:3+H]\n    \n    # We need to find a horizontal or vertical segment of length K\n    # such that the number of '.' in that segment is minimized.\n    # If a segment contains 'x', it's invalid (cannot be changed to 'o').\n    # The cost is the count of '.' in the valid segment.\n    # If no valid segment exists, output -1.\n    \n    min_ops = float('inf')\n    found_valid = False\n    \n    # Check horizontal segments\n    for i in range(H):\n        row = S[i]\n        # Sliding window of size K\n        # Count '.' and check for 'x'\n        current_dots = 0\n        has_x = False\n        \n        # Initialize first window\n        for j in range(K):\n            if row[j] == '.':\n                current_dots += 1\n            elif row[j] == 'x':\n                has_x = True\n        \n        if not has_x:\n            found_valid = True\n            min_ops = min(min_ops, current_dots)\n            \n        # Slide\n        for j in range(1, W - K + 1):\n            # Remove element at j-1\n            out_char = row[j-1]\n            # Add element at j+K-1\n            in_char = row[j+K-1]\n            \n            if out_char == '.':\n                current_dots -= 1\n            elif out_char == 'x':\n                has_x = False # Actually, we need to track if there was an x in the previous window\n                \n            # Re-evaluating sliding window logic is tricky if we just toggle flags.\n            # Better approach: reset or maintain state carefully.\n            pass\n            \n        # Let's restart the horizontal check with a cleaner sliding window\n        for i in range(H):\n            row = S[i]\n            # Window [j, j+K-1]\n            # We can iterate j from 0 to W-K\n            # Maintain count of dots and existence of x\n            \n            # Initial window\n            dots = 0\n            bad = False\n            for k_idx in range(K):\n                char = row[k_idx]\n                if char == '.':\n                    dots += 1\n                elif char == 'x':\n                    bad = True\n            \n            if not bad:\n                found_valid = True\n                min_ops = min(min_ops, dots)\n                \n            for j in range(1, W - K + 1):\n                # Remove row[j-1], add row[j+K-1]\n                out_char = row[j-1]\n                in_char = row[j+K-1]\n                \n                if out_char == 'x':\n                    bad = False # Need to check if there are other x's? No, we need to know if ANY x is in window.\n                    # This simple toggle doesn't work because removing an 'x' might leave other 'x's.\n                    # So we should probably just recount or use a frequency map/count of x's.\n                    pass\n\n    # Let's use a proper sliding window with counts\n    min_ops = float('inf')\n    found_valid = False\n    \n    # Horizontal\n    for i in range(H):\n        row = S[i]\n        x_count = 0\n        dot_count = 0\n        \n        for j in range(K):\n            if row[j] == 'x':\n                x_count += 1\n            elif row[j] == '.':\n                dot_count += 1\n                \n        if x_count == 0:\n            found_valid = True\n            min_ops = min(min_ops, dot_count)\n            \n        for j in range(1, W - K + 1):\n            out_char = row[j-1]\n            in_char = row[j+K-1]\n            \n            if out_char == 'x':\n                x_count -= 1\n            elif out_char == '.':\n                dot_count -= 1\n                \n            if in_char == 'x':\n                x_count += 1\n            elif in_char == '.':\n                dot_count += 1\n                \n            if x_count == 0:\n                found_valid = True\n                min_ops = min(min_ops, dot_count)\n\n    # Vertical\n    for j in range(W):\n        col_chars = [S[i][j] for i in range(H)]\n        x_count = 0\n        dot_count = 0\n        \n        for i in range(K):\n            if col_chars[i] == 'x':\n                x_count += 1\n            elif col_chars[i] == '.':\n                dot_count += 1\n                \n        if x_count == 0:\n            found_valid = True\n            min_ops = min(min_ops, dot_count)\n            \n        for i in range(1, H - K + 1):\n            out_char = col_chars[i-1]\n            in_char = col_chars[i+K-1]\n            \n            if out_char == 'x':\n                x_count -= 1\n            elif out_char == '.':\n                dot_count -= 1\n                \n            if in_char == 'x':\n                x_count += 1\n            elif in_char == '.':\n                dot_count += 1\n                \n            if x_count == 0:\n                found_valid = True\n                min_ops = min(min_ops, dot_count)\n\n    if not found_valid:\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(min_ops)\n\nsolve()\n```",
