    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    iterator = iter(data)\n    t = int(next(iterator))\n    \n    results = []\n    \n    for _ in range(t):\n        n = int(next(iterator))\n        k = int(next(iterator))\n        s = next(iterator)\n        \n        # We need to cover all 'B' characters with intervals of length k.\n        # Greedy approach: Find the first 'B'. To cover it, we must start an interval\n        # such that this 'B' is included. Since we want to minimize operations,\n        # we should extend the coverage as far right as possible.\n        # So, if the first 'B' is at index i, we place an operation covering [i, i+k-1].\n        # Then we continue searching for the next 'B' after this interval.\n        \n        ops = 0\n        i = 0\n        while i < n:\n            if s[i] == 'B':\n                ops += 1\n                # Apply operation starting at i, covering i to i+k-1\n                # Effectively, all B's in this range are removed.\n                # We can skip ahead to i + k because any B before i+k is covered.\n                # Specifically, the interval is [i, i+k-1]. The next unchecked position is i+k.\n                i += k\n            else:\n                i += 1\n                \n        results.append(str(ops))\n        \n    print('\\n'.join(results))\n\nsolve()\n```",
