      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef beautiful_indices(s: str, a: str, b: str, k: int) -> list[int]:\n    # Find all occurrences of a\n    a_indices = []\n    len_a = len(a)\n    for i in range(len(s) - len_a + 1):\n        if s[i:i+len_a] == a:\n            a_indices.append(i)\n    \n    # Find all occurrences of b\n    b_indices = []\n    len_b = len(b)\n    for i in range(len(s) - len_b + 1):\n        if s[i:i+len_b] == b:\n            b_indices.append(i)\n    \n    # For each index in a_indices, check if there exists an index in b_indices\n    # such that the absolute difference is <= k\n    beautiful = []\n    \n    # Since both lists are sorted, we can use binary search for efficiency\n    import bisect\n    \n    for ai in a_indices:\n        # We need a bj in b_indices such that |ai - bj| <= k\n        # This means bj >= ai - k and bj <= ai + k\n        left = bisect.bisect_left(b_indices, ai - k)\n        right = bisect.bisect_right(b_indices, ai + k) - 1\n        \n        if left <= right and left < len(b_indices):\n            beautiful.append(ai)\n    \n    return beautiful\n```",
