      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findMissingAndRepeatedValues(grid):\n    n = len(grid)\n    total = n * n\n    \n    # Flatten the grid to make processing easier\n    nums = []\n    for row in grid:\n        nums.extend(row)\n    \n    # Count occurrences of each number\n    count = {}\n    for num in nums:\n        count[num] = count.get(num, 0) + 1\n    \n    a = None  # Repeating number\n    b = None  # Missing number\n    \n    for num in range(1, total + 1):\n        if count.get(num, 0) == 2:\n            a = num\n        elif count.get(num, 0) == 0:\n            b = num\n    \n    return [a, b]\n```",
