      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nimport heapq\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    iterator = iter(input_data)\n    \n    try:\n        N = int(next(iterator))\n    except StopIteration:\n        return\n\n    # We have N-1 lines of edges, for stages 1 to N-1\n    # Each line has A_i, B_i, X_i\n    # Stage i corresponds to index i-1 in 0-based indexing for our list of choices\n    \n    # We want to find the minimum time to reach a state where we can play stage N.\n    # Initially, we can play stage 1.\n    # From stage i (1 <= i <= N-1), we can:\n    #   - Spend A_i to unlock stage i+1\n    #   - Spend B_i to unlock stage X_i\n    \n    # This is a shortest path problem on a graph.\n    # Nodes are stages 1 to N.\n    # However, \"unlocking\" a stage means we can then play it.\n    # The cost is accumulated. We start at stage 1 with cost 0.\n    # From stage i, we can go to stage i+1 with cost A_i, or to stage X_i with cost B_i.\n    # We want the minimum cost to reach stage N (i.e., be able to play stage N).\n    \n    # Note: Once we unlock a stage, we can play it. Playing it doesn't cost extra beyond the transition.\n    # The question asks for the minimum time to be able to play stage N.\n    \n    # So, we have a directed graph with nodes 1..N.\n    # For each i from 1 to N-1:\n    #   Edge i -> i+1 with weight A_i\n    #   Edge i -> X_i with weight B_i\n    \n    # We need the shortest path from node 1 to node N.\n    \n    # Since N can be up to 2*10^5, we use Dijkstra's algorithm.\n    \n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    \n    for i in range(1, N):\n        A_i = int(next(iterator))\n        B_i = int(next(iterator))\n        X_i = int(next(iterator))\n        \n        # From stage i, we can go to i+1 with cost A_i\n        adj[i].append((i + 1, A_i))\n        # From stage i, we can go to X_i with cost B_i\n        adj[i].append((X_i, B_i))\n        \n    # Dijkstra's algorithm\n    dist = [float('inf')] * (N + 1)\n    dist[1] = 0\n    pq = [(0, 1)]  # (cost, node)\n    \n    while pq:\n        d, u = heapq.heappop(pq)\n        \n        if d > dist[u]:\n            continue\n        \n        if u == N:\n            break\n            \n        for v, w in adj[u]:\n            new_dist = d + w\n            if new_dist < dist[v]:\n                dist[v] = new_dist\n                heapq.heappush(pq, (new_dist, v))\n                \n    print(dist[N])\n\nsolve()\n```",
