    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    S = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    n = len(S)\n    MOD = 998244353\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of ways to fill prefix S[0..i-1] such that the balance is j\n    # balance increases by 1 for '(', decreases by 1 for ')'\n    # For '?' it can be either.\n    # We need final balance to be 0 and intermediate balances >= 0.\n    \n    # Since n <= 3000, max balance can be up to 3000.\n    # dp[j] represents the number of ways to have balance j after processing some prefix.\n    \n    # Initialize dp array\n    # dp[j] = number of ways to reach balance j\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        char = S[i]\n        new_dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n        \n        for j in range(n + 1):\n            if dp[j] == 0:\n                continue\n            \n            if char == '(':\n                if j + 1 <= n:\n                    new_dp[j + 1] = (new_dp[j + 1] + dp[j]) % MOD\n            elif char == ')':\n                if j - 1 >= 0:\n                    new_dp[j - 1] = (new_dp[j - 1] + dp[j]) % MOD\n            else:  # char == '?'\n                # Can be '('\n                if j + 1 <= n:\n                    new_dp[j + 1] = (new_dp[j + 1] + dp[j]) % MOD\n                # Can be ')'\n                if j - 1 >= 0:\n                    new_dp[j - 1] = (new_dp[j - 1] + dp[j]) % MOD\n        \n        dp = new_dp\n    \n    # The answer is dp[0], but we must ensure that we never went below 0 balance.\n    # The DP above naturally handles this because we don't add to negative indices.\n    # However, we also need the final balance to be 0.\n    \n    print(dp[0])\n\nsolve()\n```",
