      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumSum(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    n = len(nums)\n    if n < 3:\n        return -1\n    \n    min_sum = float('inf')\n    \n    # For each potential peak j, find the minimum element to its left and right\n    # that is smaller than nums[j]\n    \n    # Precompute prefix minimums: left_min[i] = min(nums[0..i-1])\n    left_min = [float('inf')] * n\n    current_min = float('inf')\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_min = min(current_min, nums[i-1])\n        left_min[i] = current_min\n    \n    # Precompute suffix minimums: right_min[i] = min(nums[i+1..n-1])\n    right_min = [float('inf')] * n\n    current_min = float('inf')\n    for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):\n        current_min = min(current_min, nums[i+1])\n        right_min[i] = current_min\n    \n    # Iterate through each possible peak index j\n    for j in range(1, n - 1):\n        if left_min[j] < nums[j] and right_min[j] < nums[j]:\n            s = left_min[j] + nums[j] + right_min[j]\n            if s < min_sum:\n                min_sum = s\n    \n    if min_sum == float('inf'):\n        return -1\n    else:\n        return min_sum\n```",
