    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minOperations(nums):\n    from collections import Counter\n    \n    counts = Counter(nums)\n    total_ops = 0\n    \n    for count in counts.values():\n        if count == 1:\n            return -1\n        \n        # Each operation removes either 2 or 3 elements.\n        # To minimize operations, we want to maximize the use of 3s.\n        # If count % 3 == 0, we use all 3s.\n        # If count % 3 == 1, we can think of it as (count - 4) / 3 + 2 ops? \n        # Actually: \n        #   If count % 3 == 0: ops = count // 3\n        #   If count % 3 == 1: we need to remove one 4 (two 2s) and rest 3s. So ops = (count - 4) // 3 + 2\n        #   If count % 3 == 2: we remove one 2 and rest 3s. So ops = (count - 2) // 3 + 1\n        \n        if count % 3 == 0:\n            ops = count // 3\n        elif count % 3 == 1:\n            # e.g., 4 -> 2+2 (2 ops), 7 -> 3+2+2 (3 ops), 10 -> 3+3+2+2 (4 ops)\n            ops = (count - 4) // 3 + 2\n        else:  # count % 3 == 2\n            # e.g., 2 -> 2 (1 op), 5 -> 3+2 (2 ops), 8 -> 3+3+2 (3 ops)\n            ops = (count - 2) // 3 + 1\n        \n        total_ops += ops\n    \n    return total_ops\n```",
