      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef max_jumps(nums: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    n = len(nums)\n    # dp[i] represents the maximum number of jumps to reach index i from index 0\n    # Initialize with -infinity to represent unreachable, except dp[0] = 0\n    dp = [-float('inf')] * n\n    dp[0] = 0\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        if dp[i] == -float('inf'):\n            continue\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            diff = nums[j] - nums[i]\n            if -target <= diff <= target:\n                if dp[j] < dp[i] + 1:\n                    dp[j] = dp[i] + 1\n    \n    return dp[n - 1] if dp[n - 1] != -float('inf') else -1\n```",
