s verify with another approach.\nWe have 5 specified roots. We need to distribute the other 5 vertices among these 5 roots to form 5 trees.\nThis is equivalent to finding the number of functions from the set of non-root vertices to the set of all vertices, subject to constraints?\nA known result states that the number of forests on $n$ vertices with $k$ components containing specified vertices $r_1, \\dots, r_k$ is $k n^{n-k-1}$.\nHere $n=10, k=5$.\nNumber = $5 \\cdot 10^{10-5-1} = 5 \\cdot 10^4 = 50,000$.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
