      "generated_answer": "To find $P(A | B)$, we first use the law of total probability: $P(A) = P(A | B)P(B) + P(A | \\neg B)P(\\neg B)$. Given $P(A) = 1/2$, $P(B) = 1/3$, $P(\\neg B) = 2/3$, and $P(A | \\neg B) = 1/4$, we substitute these values into the equation: $1/2 = P(A | B)(1/3) + (1/4)(2/3)$. Solving for $P(A | B)$ yields $1/2 = P(A | B)/3 + 1/6$, which simplifies to $P(A | B)/3 = 1/3$, so $P(A | B) = 1$.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
