    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The total number of nodes in a complete K-ary tree of depth N is (K^(N+1) - 1)/(K-1), and the number of nonterminal (internal) nodes is (K^N - 1)/(K-1). The ratio of nonterminal nodes to total nodes simplifies to (K^N - 1)/K^(N+1) = (K^N - 1)/(K · K^N), which approaches 1/K as N grows large, and exactly equals (K-1)/K times something close to 1.\n\nLooking at the exact ratio: Nonterminal/Total = (K^N - 1)/(K^(N+1) - 1) = (K-1)/(K - 1/K^N), which for large N approaches 1/K.\n\nThe best approximation among the options is 1/K.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
