      "generated_answer": "To find $P(TP)$, we use the Law of Total Probability: $P(TP) = P(TP|D)P(D) + P(TP|\\neg D)P(\\neg D)$. Given $P(D)=0.05$, $P(TP|D)=0.99$, and $P(\\text{negative}|\\neg D)=0.97$ (so $P(TP|\\neg D)=0.03$), the calculation is $(0.99 \\times 0.05) + (0.03 \\times 0.95) = 0.0495 + 0.0285 = 0.078$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
