      "generated_answer": "The channel capacity is given by $C = \\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1 + \\text{SNR})$. Given the output power constraint $E[Y^2] \\le P_{out} = 2$ and noise variance $\\sigma_Z^2 = 1$, the maximum signal power $P_X$ satisfies $P_X + \\sigma_Z^2 \\le 2$, so $P_X \\le 1$. The SNR is therefore $P_X / \\sigma_Z^2 = 1/1 = 1$. Thus, $C = \\frac{1}{2} \\log_2(1+1) = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 = 0.5$ bits.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
