ne\" is the last element. Loop finishes. `foundIndex` = 4. Displays 4. Correct.\n\nExample D: List [\"Andrea\", \"Ben\"], Target \"Ben\".\n\"Ben\" is the last element. Loop finishes. `foundIndex` = 2. Displays 2. Correct.\n\nExample G: List [\"Andrea\", \"Ben\", \"Chris\"], Target \"Ben\".\n1. Andrea != Ben -> foundIndex = 0\n2. Ben == Ben -> foundIndex = 2\n3. Chris != Ben -> foundIndex = 0\nLoop ends. Displays 0.\nIntended result: Index of \"Ben\" is 2.\nActual result: 0.\nThis demonstrates the procedure does NOT work as intended.\n\nTherefore, Option G is the correct counter-example.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
