      "generated_answer": "An undirected graph has an Euler circuit if and only if it is connected and every vertex has an even degree. In a complete graph $K_n$, every vertex has degree $n-1$; thus, $K_{12}$ has vertices of degree 11 (odd) and $K_{13}$ has vertices of degree 12 (even). Trees with more than 2 vertices always have leaves (degree 1), so they cannot have an Euler circuit. Therefore, only statement II describes a graph that must have an Euler circuit.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
