te the exact accrued portion, but the annual dividend is fixed at $1.90625, and the yield percentage matches this annual dividend divided by the price, the most direct \"yield in dollars\" associated with the stock's performance metric is the annual dividend.\n\nHowever, often \"yield\" in these contexts can refer to the total return or the specific dollar value of the dividend component. Given the explicit statement \"annual dividends of $ 1.90625 per share\", and the calculation $23.53 * 8.101% = $1.90625, the dollar value of the yield (dividend) is $1.90625.\n\n\\boxed{1.90625}",
