  },
  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_183",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: (A) How many gallons are there in 12 liters? (B) How many liters are there in 10 quarts? Metric to Customary Units Customary to Metric Units 1 liter = 1.057 quarts .264 gallon 1 quart = .946 liter 1 gallon = 3.785 liters 1 milliliter = .0338 ounce 1 ounce = 29.57 milliliters\n\nOptions: \nA. (A) 3.168 gallons (B) 9.46 liters\nB. (A) 3.18 gallons (B) 9.6 liters\nC. (A) 2.64 gallons (B) 9.46 liters\nD. (A) 2.5 gallons (B) 9 liters\nE. (A) 2.64 gallons (B) 10.5 liters\nF. (A) 3.5 gallons (B) 9.46 liters\nG. (A) 3 gallons (B) 9.5 liters\nH. (A) 3.168 gallons (B) 10.46 liters\nI. (A) 3.168 gallons (B) 11 liters\nJ. (A) 3.2 gallons (B) 10 liters\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the number of gallons in 12 liters, we use the conversion factor $1 \\text{ gallon} = 3.785 \\text{ liters}$: $12 / 3.785 \\approx 3.17$ gallons. To find the number of liters in 10 quarts, we use the conversion factor $1 \\text{ quart} = 0.946 \\text{ liters}$: $10 \\times 0.946 = 9.46$ liters. Comparing these results to the options, Option A provides 3.168 gallons (a precise calculation using $1 \\text{ liter} = 0.264 \\text{ gallon}$ yields $12 \\times 0.264 = 3.168$) and 9.46 liters.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
