    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the regression line $Y = a + bX$ and correlation coefficient $r$, we first calculate the means $\\bar{X} = 1860/31 = 60$ and $\\bar{Y} = 465/31 = 15$. The slope $b$ is calculated as $(n\\sum XY - \\sum X \\sum Y) / (n\\sum X^2 - (\\sum X)^2) = (31(23400) - 1860(465)) / (31(201600) - 1860^2) = 134700 / 1742400 \\approx 0.0773$. Wait, let me re-calculate carefully.\nNumerator for $b$: $31 \\times 23,400 - 1,860 \\times 465 = 725,400 - 864,900 = -139,500$.\nDenominator for $b$: $31 \\times 201,600 - 1,860^2 = 6,249,600 - 3,459,600 = 2,790,000$.\nSlope $b = -139,500 / 2,790,000 = -0.05$.\nIntercept $a = \\bar{Y} - b\\bar{X} = 15 - (-0.05)(60) = 15 + 3 = 18$.\nSo the regression equation is $Y = 18 - 0.05X$.\nFor correlation $r$:\nNumerator for $r$: same as numerator for $b$ scaled? No, $r = \\frac{n\\sum XY - \\sum X \\sum Y}{\\sqrt{[n\\sum X^2 - (\\sum X)^2][n\\sum Y^2 - (\\sum Y)^2]}}$.\nDenominator part 1: $2,790,000$.\nDenominator part 2: $31(7,925) - 465^2 = 245,675 - 216,225 = 29,450$.\n$r = -139,500 / \\sqrt{2,790,000 \\times 29,450} = -139,500 / \\sqrt{82,165,500,000} \\approx -139,500 / 286,645 \\approx -0.4867$.\n\nThe correct option is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
