    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "With logarithmic utility $U(W) = \\ln(W)$, a risk-averse individual facing a fair insurance market will choose full coverage to eliminate risk. The premium for full insurance covers the expected loss ($0.5 \\times \\$10,000 = \\$5,000$), leaving the individual with a certain wealth of $\\$15,000$. The utility is therefore $\\ln(15,000) \\approx 9.6158$, which rounds to 9.616.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
