    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_177",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given that the cost of mimeographing x number of copies is C(x) = 0.005x + [(4500) / x], what is the number of copies that will minimize the cost?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2000 copies\nB. 500 copies\nC. 1200 copies\nD. 300 copies\nE. 700 copies\nF. 600 copies\nG. 1500 copies\nH. 949 copies\nI. 800 copies\nJ. 1000 copies\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\nThe cost function is \\(C(x) = 0.005x + \\frac{4500}{x}\\). To minimize the cost, find the critical point by setting the derivative \\(C'(x) = 0.005 - \\frac{4500}{x^2} = 0\\), which gives \\(x^2 = 900,000\\). Solving for \\(x\\), \\(x = \\sqrt{900,000} \\approx 949\\). The second derivative \\(C''(x) = \\frac{9000}{x^3} > 0\\) for \\(x > 0\\), confirming a minimum. Among the options, 949 copies corresponds to option H.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{H}}",
