    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_20",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: (a) Given the two discount series of 30-10-2(1/2) % and 25-15-2%, which is better? (b) Given the discount series 15-15% and the single rate of 30%, which is better?\n\nOptions: \nA. The series 30-10-2(1/2)% and the single rate of 25% are better\nB. The single rate of 25% and the series 15-15% are better\nC. The series 30-10-2(1/2) % and the series 15-15% are better\nD. The series 25-15-2% and the single rate of 30% are better\nE. The series 30-10-2(1/2)% is better, but there is no difference between the series 15-15% and the single rate of 30%\nF. Both discount series are equally beneficial\nG. The series 25-15-2% is better, and the series 15-15% and the single rate of 30% are equally beneficial\nH. The series 25-15-2% and the series 15-15% are better\nI. The series 25-15-2% and the single rate of 25% are better\nJ. The series 30-10-2(1/2) % and the single rate of 30% are better\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the better discount, we calculate the net price equivalent rate for each series. For part (a), the effective discount of 30-10-2.5% is $1 - (0.7 \\times 0.9 \\times 0.975) = 0.38575$ (38.575%), while 25-15-2% is $1 - (0.75 \\times 0.85 \\times 0.98) = 0.37525$ (37.525%); thus, the first series is better. For part (b), the effective discount of 15-15% is $1 - (0.85 \\times 0.85) = 0.2775$ (27.75%), while the single rate is 30%; since 30% > 27.75%, the single rate is better. Therefore, the series 30-10-2.5% is better in (a) and the single rate of 30% is better in (b).\n\n\\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
