      "generated_answer": "To find the average collection period, we first calculate the average accounts receivable for each year: $(28,000 + 32,000)/2 = 30,000$ for 19X1 and $(32,000 + 35,000)/2 = 33,500$ for 19X2. Next, we determine the receivables turnover ratio using sales divided by average AR, then divide 360 by this ratio to get the days: $360 / (850,000/30,000) \\approx 12.71$ days for 19X1 and $360 / (920,000/33,500) \\approx 13.11$ days for 19X2. The cost/saving is calculated on the difference in AR balance ($33,500 - 30,000 = 3,500$) multiplied by the interest rate ($10\\%$), resulting in $\\$350$, but looking at the options, Option H matches the days closely ($12.7$ and $13.11$).\n\n\\boxed{H}",
