    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For over-identified systems of simultaneous equations, Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) is biased and inconsistent, so it is not a valid estimation technique. Instrumental Variables (IV) and Two-Stage Least Squares (2SLS) are standard methods used for such systems, while Indirect Least Squares (ILS) is applicable but generally preferred for just-identified systems (though technically an option in broader contexts, it fails for over-identified ones). Therefore, the correct estimators among the choices are IV and 2SLS.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
