      "generated_answer": "To forecast volatility over a multi-day horizon in a GARCH model, one must sum the conditional variances for each day in the forecast period because variances are additive for independent increments (or under the assumption that returns are uncorrelated). The total variance for the 10-day period is the sum of the 1-day, 2-day, ..., up to the 10-day ahead conditional variance forecasts. The volatility is then obtained by taking the square root of this summed variance.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
