  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_5989",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Education makes Chris a better worker, voter, parent, and citizen. Because the benefits from education go beyond those that Chris enjoys himself, education provides\n\nOptions: \nA. no externalities and should not be subsidized\nB. decreasing marginal utility and should be taxed\nC. increasing marginal utility and should be subsidized\nD. increasing marginal utility and should not be subsidized\nE. externalities and should be taxed\nF. externalities and should not be subsidized\nG. externalities and should be subsidized\nH. increasing marginal utility and should be taxed\nI. no externalities and should be subsidized\nJ. decreasing marginal utility and should not be taxed\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
