      "generated_answer": "To determine the nature of the AR(2) process $y_t = 1.5 y_{t-1} - 0.5 y_{t-2} + u_t$, we examine the roots of its characteristic equation $\\lambda^2 - 1.5\\lambda + 0.5 = 0$. The roots are $\\lambda_1 = 1$ and $\\lambda_2 = 0.5$. Since one root lies exactly on the unit circle ($|\\lambda_1|=1$) and the other is inside ($|\\lambda_2|<1$), the process contains a unit root and is therefore non-stationary. It is not explosive because no root has a modulus greater than 1. Thus, it is best described as a unit root process.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
