      "generated_answer": "The statute creates a significant disparity in ballot access requirements, imposing a heavy burden on independent candidates and smaller political bodies while allowing established parties easier access through primaries. Under Supreme Court precedent (such as *Tashjian v. Republican Party* or *Burdick v. Takushi*), such disparate treatment constitutes an undue burden on the First Amendment right of association and the right to vote. Therefore, the court will likely find the statute unconstitutional due to this undue burden.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
