      "generated_answer": "The neighbor acquired a valid easement appurtenant (or at least an easement in gross that is transferable with the land in this context, though typically easements appurtenant run with the land) via the written deed, which satisfies the Statute of Frauds. The failure to record does not invalidate the conveyance between the parties, and non-use alone, without intent to abandon, does not terminate the easement. Since the neighbor sold Lot 2 to the professor and the easement was intended to benefit the neighboring lot (ingress/egress), the easement passed to the professor.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
