    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $\\omega = \\cos\\frac{{2\\pi}}{{7}} + i \\cdot \\sin\\frac{{2\\pi}}{{7}},$ where $i = \\sqrt{{-1}}.$ Find the value of the product\\[\\prod_{{k=0}}^6 \\left(\\omega^{{3k}} + \\omega^k + 1\\right).\\]\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1-0528-Qwen3-8B",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\nThe product \\(\\prod_{k=0}^6 (\\omega^{3k} + \\omega^k + 1)\\) is evaluated using the resultant of the polynomials \\(f(x) = x^3 + x + 1\\) and \\(g(x) = x^7 - 1\\). Since \\(g(x)\\) is monic, the resultant \\(\\text{Res}(f, g)\\) equals the product of \\(f(\\zeta)\\) for all roots \\(\\zeta\\) of \\(g(x)\\), which are the 7th roots of unity.\n\nDividing \\(g(x)\\) by \\(f(x)\\) gives a remainder \\(r(x) = 2x^2 - 2\\). Since both polynomials are monic, \\(\\text{Res}(f, g) = \\text{Res}(f, r)\\). Using the property that \\(\\text{Res}(f, c h(x)) = c^{\\deg f} \\text{Res}(f, h(x))\\) for a constant \\(c\\), \\(\\text{Res}(f, r) = 2^3 \\text{Res}(f, x^2 - 1)\\). The roots of \\(x^2 - 1\\) are \\(1\\) and \\(-1\\), so \\(\\text{Res}(f, x^2 - 1) = f(1) f(-1) = (1^3 + 1 + 1)( (-1)^3 + (-1) + 1) = 3 \\cdot (-1) = -3\\). Thus, \\(\\text{Res}(f, r) = 8 \\cdot (-3) = -24\\), and \\(\\text{Res}(f, g) = -24\\).\n\nThe product is \\(-24\\), as it equals \\(\\prod_{\\zeta^7=1} f(\\zeta)\\).\n\n\\boxed{-24}",
