      "generated_answer": "\nThe triangle \\(ABC\\) has sides \\(AB = 5\\), \\(BC = 9\\), and \\(AC = 10\\). The circumcircle \\(\\omega\\) is defined, and the tangents at \\(B\\) and \\(C\\) intersect at \\(D\\). The line \\(AD\\) intersects \\(\\omega\\) again at \\(P\\).\n\nUsing coordinate geometry, place \\(B\\) at \\((0, 0)\\), \\(C\\) at \\((9, 0)\\), and find \\(A\\) at \\(\\left(\\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{4\\sqrt{14}}{3}\\right)\\). The circumcircle equation is \\(x^2 + y^2 - 9x + E y = 0\\) with \\(E = -\\frac{66}{\\sqrt{224}}\\). The coordinates of \\(D\\) are \\(\\left(\\frac{9}{2}, -\\frac{27\\sqrt{14}}{11}\\right)\\).\n\nThe distance \\(DA = \\frac{325}{22}\\) and the power of \\(D\\) is \\(DB^2 = \\left(\\frac{225}{22}\\right)^2\\). By the power of a point, \\(DA \\cdot DP = DB^2\\), so \\(DP = \\frac{2025}{286}\\). The order of points on the line is \\(D\\), \\(P\\), \\(A\\), so \\(AP = DA - DP = \\frac{100}{13}\\).\n\nThe fraction \\(\\frac{100}{13}\\) is in simplest terms, so \\(m = 100\\), \\(n = 13\\), and \\(m + n = 113\\).\n\n\\boxed{113}",
