    "global index": "AIME_75",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Among the 900 residents of Aimeville, there are 195 who own a diamond ring, 367 who own a set of golf clubs, and 562 who own a garden spade. In addition, each of the 900 residents owns a bag of candy hearts. There are 437 residents who own exactly two of these things, and 234 residents who own exactly three of these things. Find the number of residents of Aimeville who own all four of these things.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "agnes-2.0-flash",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let $N=900$ be the total number of residents. Let $A, B, C, D$ be the sets of residents owning a diamond ring, golf clubs, garden spade, and candy hearts, respectively. We know $|A|=195$, $|B|=367$, $|C|=562$, and since everyone owns candy hearts, $|D|=900$. The sum of the sizes of these sets is $|A|+|B|+|C|+|D| = 195 + 367 + 562 + 900 = 2024$.\n\nLet $n_k$ be the number of residents who own exactly $k$ items. We are given that $n_2 = 437$ and $n_3 = 234$. Since every resident owns at least one item (candy hearts), the total population is the sum of residents owning exactly 1, 2, 3, or 4 items: $n_1 + n_2 + n_3 + n_4 = 900$. Substituting the known values, we get $n_1 + 437 + 234 + n_4 = 900$, which simplifies to $n_1 + n_4 = 229$.\n\nThe sum of the set sizes also equals the weighted sum of residents by the number of items they own: $\\sum |Set_i| = 1 \\cdot n_1 + 2 \\cdot n_2 + 3 \\cdot n_3 + 4 \\cdot n_4$. Substituting the known sums: $2024 = n_1 + 2(437) + 3(234) + 4n_4$. This simplifies to $2024 = n_1 + 874 + 702 + 4n_4$, or $2024 = n_1 + 1576 + 4n_4$, so $n_1 + 4n_4 = 448$.\n\nWe now have a system of two linear equations:\n1) $n_1 + n_4 = 229$\n2) $n_1 + 4n_4 = 448$\n\nSubtracting equation (1) from equation (2): $(n_1 + 4n_4) - (n_1 + n_4) = 448 - 229$, which gives $3n_4 = 219$. Solving for $n_4$, we find $n_4 = 73$.\n\n\\boxed{73}",
